    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form across the stack so the app satisfies the spec while staying backward-compatible.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (inherited by the `Owner` response schema via `allOf`).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only request (no flat `address`) is accepted at the bean-validation layer. `city`/`telephone` remain required.\n- Documented that the response `address` is the composed, normalized value.\n\n**Domain model** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (mapped to `address_line1`/`address_line2`) with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them in both directions, so the response DTO carries them.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added the two nullable columns to all four schema files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`); the hsqldb one is what the tests actually use (`ddl-auto=none`).\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)\n- Prefers the structured fields when `addressLine1` is non-blank, else falls back to the flat `address`.\n- Normalizes whichever fields are supplied (same trim/collapse/upper-case/`ST\u2192STREET` rules).\n- Composes the stored/returned `address` as normalized `addressLine1`, appending a single space + normalized `addressLine2` when line 2 is present.\n- Validity requires an address in either form (non-blank `addressLine1` or flat `address`) plus city \u2014 the existing `isBlank(address)` missing-field check now covers both forms since `address` is derived first.\n- Persists the normalized `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (null when the flat form was used).\n\nSince city and postcode are already independent top-level fields shared by both forms, the household hash, postcode validation, and locality derivations continue to read the correct structured values with no further change.",
